{
  "requirement": "Each assessment MUST have a separate JSON usage record under\n`<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` using\n{cite}`requirements.configuration.state_location`.\nIt MUST identify its format version, run, project root, subject kind and full\nname, start time, backend and model when known, end time when finished, outcome,\naccepted determination kind (`true`, `false`, or `FIXME`) when present, and\nwhether evidence was written. It MUST record the selected output destination in\n`evidence_output` as `file` or `stdout`; a successful write to either destination\nMUST set `evidence_written` to true. Usage recording MUST remain outside the\nproject in stdout mode. FIXME entry text MUST NOT be stored in usage records.\nFailed, cancelled, or unfinished\nruns MUST remain distinguishable from completed judgments. Records MUST persist\nfor later review without storing source text, prompts, responses, or rationale.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.authoring.usage_storage`. I did not request implementation source.\n\n**Location and identity (cites `requirements.configuration.state_location`)**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` finds exactly one record under `<state>/habeas/authoring/usage/`. It checks that the file is named `<run_id>.json`.\n- A second `--force` run leaves the first record byte-identical and adds a separate second file, so each assessment gets its own record.\n- The same test checks these fields:\n  - `version`, `project_root`, `subject`, `subject_kind`, `backend` and `model`.\n  - `evidence_output == \"file\"`.\n  - `start_time_ms` and `end_time_ms`, with start no later than end.\n- The same test covers an unusable or undeterminable state root. It runs with `XDG_STATE_HOME` pointing at a file and with `XDG_STATE_HOME` and `HOME` unset. Both runs fail with a stderr message, and no evidence is changed.\n- `citation_reviews_are_confirmed_with_fresh_targeted_conversations` checks that each assessment writes its own usage file with a distinct `run_id`. `confirm_runs_a_second_assessment_with_its_own_usage_record` checks the same for confirm runs.\n- `usage_subject_kind_is_known_before_sources_are_prepared` covers the four subject kinds: requirement, example, citation review and site review. It also covers an unknown subject. `usage_record_of_an_early_failure_identifies_its_subject_kind` checks that an early failure still records `subject_kind` and a null backend and model.\n\n**Determination kind and `evidence_written`**\n- `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files` covers `true`, `false` and `FIXME` in stdout mode. It asserts `usage.determination == kind`, `evidence_output == \"stdout\"`, `evidence_written == true` and `outcome == \"completed\"`.\n- `false_is_a_completed_assessment` asserts `determination == \"false\"` and a completed outcome.\n- `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` asserts the `FIXME` kind, `evidence_written == true` and a completed outcome for a file write.\n- `live_bedrock_authoring` also asserts `evidence_output == \"stdout\"` and `evidence_written == true`, but it is skipped when `CI` is set.\n\n**Usage stays outside the project in stdout mode**\n- `usage_state_inside_the_project_is_refused_before_creating_it` runs both default and `--stdout` modes with the state root inside the project. It asserts a refusal message, empty stdout, no state directory created and evidence unchanged.\n\n**Failed, cancelled and unfinished runs remain distinguishable**\n- `unfinished_runs_are_visible_before_the_backend_is_selected` checks `outcome == \"unfinished\"`, null end time, backend and model, and `evidence_written == false`.\n- `missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence` covers file and stdout modes. It asserts `failed`, `evidence_output`, `evidence_written == false` and a null determination.\n- `failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage` asserts `failed`, `FIXME` and `evidence_written == false`.\n- `failed_assessment_keeps_other_results_and_reports_failure` and `a_denied_mandatory_input_aborts_only_its_assessment` check failed records alongside completed ones.\n- `failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause` covers both `failed` and `cancelled` outcomes. It asserts a set end time, a null determination and `evidence_written == false`. It also covers an obstructed usage path.\n- `interrupted_terminal_progress_keeps_unstarted_work_incomplete` covers the interrupted batch.\n\n**Content-free records**\n- The Ollama CLI test asserts that the serialized usage record contains none of `SECRET_REQUIREMENT_TEXT`, `SECRET_DEFINITION_TEXT`, `SECRET_SOURCE_PAYLOAD`, `SECRET_RATIONALE`, the credential or `#125`. The `#125` check covers the FIXME entry text. It also asserts `github_issues` is absent from the usage record.\n- `authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file` asserts the literal API key is absent from usage.\n\nNo obligation lacks a test with a relevant assertion, and I found no plausible violating behavior the tests would accept.",
  "references": "8c266bd14ae66b5b7651841b71fae50faddc6c6ad08ec107580bad7462d9a96b",
